From dca8ddd60c46e9e40c0604efff6d86bdaa4dd2bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:27:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 24/36] PS2: cache rendered DrawStringFormat text per texture

DrawStringFormat and DrawStringFormat2 re-rendered the same string into
the same texture every frame (two TTF renders and two texture uploads
per call, and the upload invalidates the whole texture in VRAM). Each
texture now keeps the key of its last text write. The key is reused only
when the inputs match and no other texture write happened since
(textureWriteGen, bumped by every SetTextureImage/SetTextureSubImage in
AnmManager). DrawTextToSprite invalidates the destination's key, so
DrawVmTextFmt writes cannot leave a stale key behind. PS2 only; not
measured on hardware or in PCSX2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019yH2brr5GjCGyCE62bYyXR
